  "content": {
    "id": "p30-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Consider the function $f:[0,\\infty)\\to\\mathbb{R}$ where $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}$. Restrict the codomain of $f$ to obtain a new function that has an inverse.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Restrict the codomain to $[0,\\infty)$: $g:[0,\\infty)\\to[0,\\infty)$ where $g(x)=\\sqrt{x}$.",
      "worked": "The range of $f$ is $[0,\\infty)$. Restrict its codomain to this range:\n$$g:[0,\\infty)\\to[0,\\infty),\\qquad g(x)=\\sqrt{x}.$$\nThe function $g$ is injective and surjective, so it is bijective and has an inverse.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 24
